WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.712
The tyrant has fallen and Iraq is free.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.340
In 2003, George W. Bush

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.710
famously declared victory in Iraq.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.130
A powerful explosion

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.188
killed more than 20 people today.

00:00:14.188 --> 00:00:15.930
The city has been in a state of chaos.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.390
Deadliest strike against American forces.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.920
Bodies have been found,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.607
policemen's, security officers'.

00:00:21.607 --> 00:00:22.980
Car exploded today

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.450
in the Iraqi city of Basra.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.880
Rockets attacks are a daily occurrence.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.190
What was considered liberation in Iraq

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.360
is beginning to look more
and more like occupation.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.760
18 years later, an estimated
half a million Iraqis,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.700
and 6,840 U.S. troops have
perished in the conflict.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.510
Today, the U.S. has 2,500 troops in Iraq,

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:46.140
down from a peak of a 168,000 in 2007.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.390
In July, the government
claimed that American troops

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.110
will no longer engage in combat;

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.060
instead, they'll only train and
assist Iraqi security forces

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.740
in their fight against ISIS.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.450
This is just diplomatic theater.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.880
The Iraqi parliament, which
has voted for the U.S.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.027
to leave the country, points
out that renaming combat troops

00:01:02.027 --> 00:01:04.380
"trainers and advisers" is deceptive.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.790
It also won't prevent the conflict

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.010
from once again escalating

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.310
into a cycle of violence and retaliation.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:11.850
The U.S. military is still
engaging in air strikes,

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:15.410
and in April, after militias
attacked five U.S. facilities,

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:16.680
the Biden administration

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.790
made good on its promise to hit back.

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:20.950
The U.S. should withdraw
all troops from Iraq

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:23.550
and finally end this disastrous war.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.080
Our presence in the country
has done the opposite

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.760
of its stated goal of
providing safety and security

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.670
in the region.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.690
I was born in Iraq and lived
through Saddam's regime,

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:35.530
Operation Desert Storm, U.S. sanctions,

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:38.970
Operation Iraqi Freedom,
and the Iraqi Civil War.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.700
I witnessed first hand how U.S.
actions that favor one group

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.850
repeatedly angered another group,

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.220
which is why the war has been

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:48.334
an endless game of whack a mole.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.270
I think a moral obligation, to be sure

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.270
that when we leave Iraq,
we leave it better off

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.350
than we found it.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.570
In 2003, L. Paul Bremer,

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:58.440
who was head of the Coalition
Provisional Authority of Iraq,

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.680
disbanded the army, which was
the most disastrous decision

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.300
in the course of the conflict.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.800
The 25-person Interim
Governing Council he created

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.070
was designed to represent

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.200
the diversity of Iraq's population,

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.300
but all it did was augment the complexity

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.560
of Iraq's ethnic and religious groups;

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.240
the result was inflaming
sectarian tensions,

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.950
which led to a deadly civil war.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.750
The region surrounding
it is even more complex.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.340
Numerous nations have competed for decades

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:25.970
throughout the greater Middle East,

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:29.340
from Iran to Saudi Arabia,
Turkey, Qatar, and more.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.090
When the U.S. removed Saddam,

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.820
it allowed these foreign interests

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.210
to work through proxies within Iraq,

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:38.580
much as they have in Yemen,
Syria, Lebanon, and Libya.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.430
For the U.S. to bring stability to Iraq,

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.030
it would need to establish peace

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.200
in the entire region as well.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.160
First, all the Sunni majority nations

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.520
would need to reconcile with themselves,

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.850
then the Sunni nations with
Iran and Iran's proxies.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.360
But as long as the U.S. remains in Iraq,

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.310
it's destined to favor
one side over another,

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.400
and will only exacerbate
the regional conflicts.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.330
The decision by the U.S. to back the Kurds

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:03.970
and the Iraqi mobilization forces

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:07.260
in their battle against
ISIS may appear successful,

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.490
but changing the region's balance of power

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:11.930
has caused new threats to emerge.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:13.270
This situation is analogous

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.400
to the U.S. experience in Afghanistan:

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.840
We supported the Mujahideen
against the Soviets,

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.890
only to see those same Mujahideen

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:23.450
and their Pakistani backers
take full control of the country

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.180
and become new adversaries

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.740
in the form of the Taliban and Al Qaeda.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.350
Similarly, in Iraq,
after the fall of ISIS,

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.090
the Iranian-backed militias
that had worked with the U.S.,

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.330
gained new influence within Iraq.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.400
And the U.S. presence in the
region encouraged other nations

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.730
to launch their own military operations.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.800
Turkey started bombing Syrian Kurds,

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.120
Saudi Arabia and the UAE joined
forces and attacked Yemen,

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.180
and the Iranianbacked
militia Kitaib Hezbollah

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.430
was caught using American-made equipment

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.860
that the U.S. had given
to the Iraqi military.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.540
The result was to strengthen Iran,

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:59.230
just as Operation Iraqi
Freedom had done back in 2003.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.810
So the U.S. switched its focus

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:02.770
to containing Iranian influence,

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.780
even assassinating Qassem Soleimani

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.370
and Abu Mahdi AlMuhandis,

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.420
whose militia was largely responsible

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.170
for the defeat of ISIS.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:12.010
This farce won't end

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:15.060
until there's a complete U.S.
withdrawal from the country.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.780
The U.S. says it's sticking around

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:19.180
to support the Iraqi
military and government,

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.370
even though each has publicly stated

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.300
that they want the Americans to leave.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.740
There's nothing stopping
Bush's disastrous war

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.310
from going on for another 18 years

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.660
in an endless loop of military actions,

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.080
followed by unintended consequences,

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:34.670
followed by a military response

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:37.220
to deal with those
unintended consequences,

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.900
followed by more unintended consequences.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.840
After 18 years, it's time
to give up on the hope

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:46.270
that U.S. troops can bring
peace and stability to Iraq.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:49.020
It's time to bring them all home.

